    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0875" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg765"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Hirsch.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 20,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 90.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Dispatch No. 123 of the 3d instant from
                    your legation is received. Your note of the 1st instant to the minister of
                    state, in the case of the assault on Messrs. Knapp and Raynolds by Moussa Bey in
                    1883, is regarded as a most excellent presentation of the matter as it stands at
                    this juncture.</p>
                <p>Awaiting the reply of the Porte,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
